{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For what great nation is there that has Elohim so near to it.</b> Moses hints to us in this verse about the preeminence of Israel: that they pray and are answered when they direct their intention toward the supernal power to influence its force into the attributes, in each and every attribute as they need it, and therefore they are answered each and every time. And he said 'a great nation' and did not say 'a holy nation' or 'a righteous nation,' because greatness is חסד (lovingkindness) and חסד is the first of the attributes; and the meaning of the verse is: for what great nation is there that has the attributes near to it, as YHWH our Elohim in all our calling to Him — and not to the attributes. And from this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, say: 'He stands up from the throne of judgment and sits upon the throne of mercy; He stands up from the throne of mercy and sits upon the throne of judgment' — all according to what the one who prays needs. And concerning the attributes the prophet, peace be upon him, said (Habakkuk 3:8): ״כי תרכב על סוסיך מרכבותיך ישועה״, and the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: it is not the rider who is subsidiary to the horse, but the horse that is subsidiary to the rider. And understand this." "<b>And know</b> that in this verse the name גדול yields two letters together with the last one, and likewise all of them in this order. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'that has Elohim near' — in every kind of nearness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:14.373020322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}